# MECHANISM PIN — the `admits` block must PRECEDE the facts it closes over.
#
# Fixture INLINE (mechanism pin). Companion to `closed-vocabulary.nibli`, split out
# because it needs a KB where an ordinary fact lands FIRST.
#
# The hazard is the mirror image of `derived_only`'s "comes too late": a `derived_only`
# placed below its facts protects nothing, and an `admits` placed below its facts
# silently GRANDFATHERS everything above it — so the vocabulary a reader counts in the
# file is not the vocabulary the engine closed. Both are false greens that load at zero
# errors and look exactly like working closures, which is why this rejects rather than
# warns. Ordering is load-bearing, and enforced rather than merely documented.
person(Adam).

:refuse reasoning /comes too late/
admits("person").

# The refusal is ATOMIC: the rejected declaration left nothing behind, so the KB is still
# open and an ordinary assertion still lands.
:accept
rich(Bela).

:expect-pins 2
